    "1000 mixed operations execute actual C initializer, malloc and release on the source side, with no stock-code fallback. Full pool images, metadata and payload-clear write width/order/value match. The existing C fill body/relocations equal its normal-build body and its unit object is unchanged.",
    "Returning paths check saved integer/FP registers, SP, masks/FPSCR and guards. Terminal paths check guards, FP/masks and stable repeated-delay stack depth; private active saved-register values and absolute private frame depth are excluded. Caller scratch/APSR excluded throughout.",
    "Status publication, typed logging, watchdog feed, RTOS flags and delay are modeled ports. Real manager event dispatch/reset, watchdog timing, scheduler concurrency, physical memory faults and boot remain unverified.",
    "Selected bounded requests and selected high signed-bit cases are tested. Near-wrap huge requests that would clear outside mapped RAM are not claimed physically verified; no extra production guard is introduced.",
    "One new C unit, no new state or final import changes. The first intermediate build exposed manager signaling; the final reviewed build includes its C bridge. Source plan/cache layout unchanged. Reallocation/deinitialization and complete source-linked firmware remain open."
  ],
